<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sicilian Vespers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1282</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as War of the Sicilian Vespers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sicilian Vespers was the uprising that began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> at Easter 1282 against the rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles I of Anjou</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. The island offered its crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon">Peter III of Aragon</a>, starting a long war between Angevins and Aragonese that split the old kingdom into a mainland part ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and an island kingdom of Sicily.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers.jpg" alt="Sicilian Vespers" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Villani · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sicilian_Vespers_1281_How_and_after_what_manner_the_island_of_Sicily_rebelled_against_King_Charles_Nuova_Cronica_Giovanni_Villani_14th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
